review_comments:
Lets say they do something like:
```c#
hubConnection.On("Reset", async () =>
{
    await hubConnection.StopAsync();
    await hubConnection.StartAsync();
});
```

With the current version of the PR it will work, however if we wait for the handlers to complete when start is called this would hang still.

I'm still leaning towards not waiting for this task anywhere. There shouldn't be any issues in the library code with previous `.On` handlers running. There could be customers who expect a certain order of operations or something and they could be surprised I guess.
